<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{.Title}}</title>
<meta name="description" content="loop is a single Go binary with both halves of building software: chat rooms of AI personas that speak up when their perspective matters, and deterministic YAML pipelines that run the work exactly as written.">
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="{{.Root}}assets/favicon.svg?v=3">
<link rel="alternate icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="{{.Root}}assets/favicon-32.png?v=3">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{.Root}}site.css">
</head>
<body>
<nav>
  <a class="brand" href="{{.Root}}index.html"><span class="brand-mark"></span>loop</a>
  <a href="{{.Root}}docs/"{{if eq .Active "docs"}} class="on"{{end}}>docs</a>
  <span class="spacer"></span>
  <a class="gh" href="https://github.com/shafi-/loop" title="github">{{template "ghicon"}}</a>
</nav>

<div class="landing">
  <header class="hero">
    <h1>Before code, a planning room.<br><span class="accent">After the plan, a pipeline.</span></h1>
    <p class="sub">loop is a single Go binary that carries both halves of building
    software. Think an idea through with a room of AI personas — each one speaks
    up only when its perspective matters — then run the implementation as a YAML
    pipeline that does <em>exactly</em> what you wrote, pausing for your approval
    at the checkpoints you define.</p>
    <div class="install">
      <code id="install-cmd">curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/shafi-/loop/main/install.sh | sh</code>
      <button id="copy-install" type="button" aria-label="copy install command">copy</button>
    </div>
    <p class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn primary" href="{{.Root}}docs/">read the docs</a>
      <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/shafi-/loop">source &amp; stars</a>
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="shot-frame">
    <div class="shot-bar">
      <span></span><span></span><span></span>
      <em>loop ui — a room, live in the browser</em>
    </div>
    <img src="assets/room.png" alt="A loop room: persona agents replying in chat, the pipeline's live status, and an approval gate.">
  </section>

  <section class="features">
    <h2>Two halves, one idea</h2>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Rooms</h3>
      <p>Personas, not a lone chatbot. Tag <code>@name</code> and that agent
      must reply; untagged ones read along and speak only when their
      perspective truly matters — silence comes with a receipt, never an
      excuse. Rooms command real pipelines: status streams into the
      conversation, and approval gates ask you right there in the chat.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Pipelines</h3>
      <p>Work as YAML: ordered stages — LLM steps, tool-running agents, human
      checkpoints, deterministic routing — executed exactly as written, with a
      full audit trail and resume from the exact point a run stopped. Even
      free-form answers at a checkpoint route deterministically.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Runs that outlive your terminal</h3>
      <p>With <code>loop serve</code>, every run is a background process: close
      the session and the work continues, and a question asked by any run is
      answerable from anywhere — the browser dashboard, another terminal, or a
      hosted room. Entirely optional: plain <code>loop run</code> stays
      zero-setup.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="quickstart">
    <h2>Two minutes to first run</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p><strong>Install and onboard</strong> — the onboarding command checks your
        provider config and installs the agent executor (no Node.js needed afterward):</p>
        <pre>loop setup</pre>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p><strong>Set one key</strong> — provider, model, and endpoint all resolve from it:</p>
        <pre>export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-...   # or OPENAI_API_KEY</pre>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p><strong>Scaffold a workspace and run your first pipeline</strong>:</p>
        <pre>loop init
loop run pipelines/feature-delivery.yaml</pre>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p><strong>Open a planning room</strong> — or run the whole thing as a service:</p>
        <pre>loop chat rooms/leadership.yaml "We need a new drone shoot-out"
# or: loop serve  +  loop ui   →  http://127.0.0.1:8787</pre>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="examples">
    <h2>The full story, end to end</h2>
    <div class="card">
      <h3><a href="https://github.com/shafi-/loop/tree/main/examples/agency-intake">agency-intake →</a></h3>
      <p>A fuzzy client request walks into a room. An intake team — account
      lead, strategist, estimator — interrogates it until the brief is
      settled, and the room's transcript becomes the input of a delivery
      pipeline. Judgment first, determinism after.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3><a href="https://github.com/shafi-/loop/tree/main/examples/incident-room">incident-room →</a></h3>
      <p>An incident response team — commander, SRE, comms lead — debates
      around a gated mitigation pipeline, and the SRE reads the last run's
      artifacts before trusting the fix. Five minutes, one key.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<footer>
  <span>loop — MIT licensed</span>
  <span class="spacer"></span>
  <a href="https://github.com/shafi-/loop" title="github">{{template "ghicon"}}</a>
  <a href="{{.Root}}docs/">docs</a>
</footer>

<script>
document.getElementById("copy-install").addEventListener("click", function () {
  var b = this;
  navigator.clipboard.writeText(document.getElementById("install-cmd").textContent)
    .then(function () { b.textContent = "copied ✓"; setTimeout(function () { b.textContent = "copy"; }, 1600); });
});
</script>
</body>
</html>
